/*
========================================================
DISPATCHER INHERITANCE & OVERRIDE — COMPLETE THEORY
========================================================

1️⃣ Core Rule (Golden Rule ⭐)
-----------------------------
A child coroutine inherits the parent's dispatcher
UNLESS it explicitly overrides it.

-----------------------------------------------

2️⃣ What gets inherited?
------------------------
From parent coroutine:
- Dispatcher
- Job
- CoroutineContext elements

ChildContext = ParentContext + ChildOverrides

-----------------------------------------------

3️⃣ Inheritance applies to ALL coroutine builders
------------------------------------------------
These ALL follow IDENTICAL rules:
✅ launch
✅ async
✅ runBlocking

There is NO difference in:
- inheritance
- override
- dispatcher selection

-----------------------------------------------

4️⃣ Difference between launch / async / runBlocking
---------------------------------------------------
launch:
- Fire-and-forget
- Returns Job
- NON-blocking

async:
- Returns Deferred<T>
- Used when result is needed
- NON-blocking (until await)

runBlocking:
- BLOCKS the current thread
- Used mainly for tests / main()
- ❗ Avoid on Android UI thread

⚠️ Dispatcher rules remain SAME for all three

-----------------------------------------------

5️⃣ Override behavior
---------------------
If dispatcher is explicitly specified:
- Parent dispatcher is IGNORED
- Child runs on specified dispatcher

Example:
launch(IO) {
    async(Default) { } // Override
}

-----------------------------------------------

6️⃣ Multi-level inheritance
---------------------------
Inheritance flows DOWNWARD:

Parent(IO)
 └─ Child(Default)   // override
     └─ GrandChild() // inherits Default

-----------------------------------------------

7️⃣ Thread vs Dispatcher (Very Important)
-----------------------------------------
Dispatcher ≠ Thread

- Dispatcher controls THREAD POOL
- Same dispatcher can use DIFFERENT threads
- Thread name change ≠ dispatcher change

-----------------------------------------------

8️⃣ Main Dispatcher Rule
-----------------------
Dispatchers.Main:
- Always runs on UI thread
- Single-threaded
- Used for UI updates ONLY

-----------------------------------------------

9️⃣ Common misconceptions ❌
-----------------------------
❌ async always runs in background
❌ launch decides dispatcher differently
❌ runBlocking changes inheritance rules
❌ same dispatcher means same thread

✅ All false

-----------------------------------------------

🔟 Android Best Practice
------------------------
Avoid:
GlobalScope.launch { }

Prefer:
lifecycleScope.launch { }
viewModelScope.launch { }

NOTE:
Dispatcher inheritance rules DO NOT change

-----------------------------------------------

ONE-LINE SUMMARY ⭐
------------------
"Dispatcher inheritance & override rules are
IDENTICAL for launch, async, and runBlocking."

========================================================
END OF THEORY
========================================================
*/
